WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.430
Everyone loves a good story. Today you will learn to tell one so your listeners hang on every word.

2
00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.790
Every story has three parts.

3
00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.930
The beginning tells who and where.

4
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:15.030
The middle has a problem, and the end shows how it is solved.

5
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:21.990
First, then, next and finally help listeners follow the order.

6
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:25.580
They are like stepping stones through your story.

7
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.060
Once upon a time and one day are great ways to begin.

8
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:32.050
Stories happened in the past, so we change the verbs.

9
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.690
Many just add -ed: look becomes looked, and drop becomes dropped.

10
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:40.630
Some change completely: go becomes went, see becomes saw.

11
00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:45.350
Change your voice for different characters.

12
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.260
Slow down at the exciting part.

13
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.900
Use your face and hands to show feelings.

14
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.200
Listen to the story of the thirsty crow.

15
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.020
Once upon a time, on a hot summer day, a crow was very thirsty.

16
00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:04.850
First, he flew everywhere looking for water. Then he saw a pot with a little water at the bottom.

17
00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.220
Next, he dropped pebbles into the pot, one by one.

18
00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.930
Finally, the water came up, and he drank happily. The end.

19
00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:16.050
Here is the story map. At the beginning, we meet a thirsty crow on a hot day.

20
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.920
In the middle, there is a problem. The water is too low to reach.

21
00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.120
He has a clever idea. He drops pebbles into the pot.

22
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.510
At the end, the water rises and he drinks. The lesson is, think hard and never give up.

23
00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:35.720
Many verbs just add ed for the past. Look, looked. Drop, dropped. Walk, walked.

24
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:42.190
Some verbs are special and change completely. Go becomes went. See becomes saw.

25
00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:45.520
Fly becomes flew, and drink becomes drank. These special verbs need practice.

26
00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:50.710
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

27
00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.240
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
